  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Calinerie, on avenue de Provence in Fréjus, is the oldest grooming salon in Fréjus and Saint-Raphaël according to its official website: founded in 1983, taken over by Thierry in 1996 and renovated in 2016 for the animals' comfort. Each dog is groomed one-on-one, entirely by Thierry himself, and the work is done in full view of the public — a deliberate transparency. Well rated, between 4.5 and 4.6/5 depending on the platform (30 to 58 reviews depending on the source).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The salon is open Monday to Friday, from 9am to 12:30pm then 2 to 5pm. Free parking on site. For a dog over 20kg, pricing is by quote. An appointment is recommended, especially during the tourist season when slots fill up fast.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book before arriving in Fréjus if you'll be there in summer — groomers in the area are often fully booked in July-August.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Fréjus town centre is accessible from avenue de Provence.</p>
